      "title": "falcodump: Exit with success if there are no interfaces",
      "message": "falcodump: Exit with success if there are no interfaces\n\nThe tests expect a successful return code even if there are on\ninterfaces (even if the \"always_present\" is false.) That's what\nandroiddump does.\n\nBoth should perhaps return a special exit code for no interfaces\n(WS_EXIT_NO_INTERFACES), though the extcap tests harness would need\nto be changed to allow that exit code when no interfaces are\nallowed.\n\nThis keeps tests from failing, e.g. on the Windows packages.\n",
